  "category": "Ancient",
  "blurb": "A steep stepped platform carrying a windowed shrine on a flat deck.",
  "teach": "Where the Mayan pack steps gently and finishes in a small hipped shrine, this one is steep and finishes FLAT: a tall rise on a short run, and a height cap that stops the offset walk before it closes to a ridge. What the cap leaves is a tread - a level deck - and that deck is the temple platform. It is also what lets the parapet work: a parapet needs something to stand on, and a roof that closes to a point has nothing.",
